+# Candidate <ID> / frozen version <N>
+
+## Opportunity and success counterfactual
+What limitation, anomaly, construction or reformulation motivates it? If it works, what important consequence follows? What could extend beyond this example, and on what assumptions?
+
+## Mechanism
+State and actual execution; formation/learning and its signal; retention or composition if claimed. Explicit scaffolding and the hardest unresolved operator. Established components are permitted.
+
+## Concrete instance
+Worked execution, derivation or minimal prototype. State which pieces are designed versus acquired. A simple case need not prove the broad claim.
+
+Full relevant discovery, construction, execution and maintenance costs, with included/excluded resources:
+
+## Closest rival and prior work
+The strongest simple alternative under the same information, feedback, resource and locality constraints. State what remains different and the limits of the search. Do not use universal simulation as an equivalence proof.
+
+## Discriminating consequence
+The observation, derivation or intervention that would change the central judgment; required cost accounting. No requirement to have the final test solved before inventing the idea.
+
+## Decision and lineage
+Main / high-risk alternative / reconstruct / pause / close, with scientific reason. Sources actually read, frozen parent, evidence and changes. Distinguish engineering repairs from mechanism changes.
